\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let G be a loopless multigraph on 2m vertices and x in its perfect-matching polytope. Is the maximum entropy H(x) of a distribution of perfect matchings having edge marginals x between $F(x)-(2-2/m)B(x)$ and F(x), where $F(x)=-\sum _e$ $x_e$ $\log (x_e)$ and B is the sum of $-(1-x_e)\log (1-x_e)$? Natural logarithms are used and 0 log 0 is zero.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let G be a loopless multigraph on 2m vertices and x in its perfect-matching polytope. Is the maximum entropy H(x) of a distribution of perfect matchings having edge marginals x between $F(x)-(2-2/m)B(x)$ and F(x), where $F(x)=-\sum _e$ $x_e$ $\log (x_e)$ and B is the sum of $-(1-x_e)\log (1-x_e)$? Natural logarithms are used and 0 log 0 is zero.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

