\section*{Entropy bounds at perfect-matching marginals}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 113; 2026-09-23), the asserted result is that feasible perfect-matching marginals satisfy the sharp entropy comparison $F-(2-2/m)B\le H\le F$, together with the face bound $|\operatorname{supp}x|-\dim F_x\le3m-2$.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 113; 2026-09-23), tight odd cuts are uncrossed and contracted to bound the tangent-space codimension. A finite exponential family on the minimal face then turns covariance trace and second-variation estimates into the entropy bound, including boundary marginals.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 113; 2026-09-23).

\subsection{Formal verification}
For manuscript 1 (family 113; 2026-09-23), the documented Lean scope is the sharp matching entropy comparison, boundary cases, and a triangle-expansion face identity; the general sharp face-dimension bound is not among the selected declarations.

The selected statement includes the clause used for this problem.

The linked family Comparator checks are \texttt{BinaryMatching.lean}, \texttt{MatchingEntropy.lean}, \texttt{MatchingEntropyBounds.lean}, \texttt{MatchingFPRAS.lean}, \texttt{SingletonLoopMatching.lean}, \texttt{TriangleFace.lean}.

Their named declarations include \texttt{OAI.BinaryMatching.deterministic\_approximate\_counting}, \texttt{OAI.LoopMatching.fullEndpoint}, \texttt{OAI.MatchingEntropy.entropy\_main}, \texttt{OAI.MatchingEntropyBounds.Refined.pointwise\_entropy}, \texttt{OAI.MatchingFPRAS.thm\_main}, \texttt{OAI.TriangleFace198.triangle\_expansion\_face}.

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

